(3805353, 534935, 68504, '<td valign="top">Hmmmmm, yes. A negative of overexposed image.  Seemed to amplify "howl" aspect, being dark.  Pure in the sense that Gus''s whole body was focused on the howl (actually a ''woof''), seeming more together as a dog than usually, for he is a gangly always cogitating sort of dog.  Thank you all for commenting and voting.</td>', 'Hmmmmm, yes. A negative of overexposed image.  Seemed to amplify "howl" aspect, being dark.  Pure in the sense that Gus''s whole body was focused on the howl (actually a ''woof''), seeming more together as a dog than usually, for he is a gangly always cogitating sort of dog.  Thank you all for commenting and voting.', '2007-06-20 02:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3805357, 535353, 50641, '<td valign="top">Very cool capture.</td>', 'Very cool capture.', '2007-06-20 02:31:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3805391, 534692, 31403, '<td valign="top">of course something with actual professional commercial value wouldn''t score as well as it deserves.  Heaven forbid we learn to make money with our cameras, or reward those that show us the way on DPC!  :)<br/> <br/>Love this, and sincerely appreciate you taking time to explain how you did it.  I''ll be setting this up in studio to try myself in the next week or so.<br/> <br/>Thanks for your contributions to this site.</td>', 'of course something with actual professional commercial value wouldn''t score as well as it deserves.  Heaven forbid we learn to make money with our cameras, or reward those that show us the way on DPC!  :) Love this, and sincerely appreciate you taking time to explain how you did it.  I''ll be setting this up in studio to try myself in the next week or so. Thanks for your contributions to this site.', '2007-06-20 02:36:59.000000', NULL, 0),
