(3807289, 533842, 66384, '<td valign="top">My guess about the score is along the lines with what Raish said. I''m guessing that many voters thought you had "shoehorned" a shot in to the Pure challenge by putting "Pure" in the title. They probably would not have had any notion of "pure" if they looked at the shot without the title.<br/> <br/>BTW the thing that keeps grabbing my attention is the girl on the right who is looking back with that other hand on her arm. There seems to be more going on there than in the rest of the picture. If that is not your focal point, you might want to crop her out.</td>', 'My guess about the score is along the lines with what Raish said. I''m guessing that many voters thought you had "shoehorned" a shot in to the Pure challenge by putting "Pure" in the title. They probably would not have had any notion of "pure" if they looked at the shot without the title. BTW the thing that keeps grabbing my attention is the girl on the right who is looking back with that other hand on her arm. There seems to be more going on there than in the rest of the picture. If that is not your focal point, you might want to crop her out.', '2007-06-20 11:26:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807292, 533526, 7743, '<td valign="top">I think the image does say ''Pure Passion (for Jazz)'' however I think the pole going through the man''s head and the limited contrast between the head and the background have let this image down.</td>', 'I think the image does say ''Pure Passion (for Jazz)'' however I think the pole going through the man''s head and the limited contrast between the head and the background have let this image down.', '2007-06-20 11:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807336, 533526, 32767, '<td valign="top">I''d say you missed the essence of the Challenge while your shots does meet it in anoutside way.<br/> <br/>If I took a picture of a guy that I know, who lied all the time...never told the truth and titled my shot "A Pure Bullshitter". Sure, it may be true and he may be pure in that but it''s not what the Challenges voters were looking for.</td>', 'I''d say you missed the essence of the Challenge while your shots does meet it in anoutside way. If I took a picture of a guy that I know, who lied all the time...never told the truth and titled my shot "A Pure Bullshitter". Sure, it may be true and he may be pure in that but it''s not what the Challenges voters were looking for.', '2007-06-20 11:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807404, 530964, 51538, '<td valign="top">Nice to see that expensive lens perform in such a gratifying way ;-) in your capable hands.</td>', 'Nice to see that expensive lens perform in such a gratifying way ;-) in your capable hands.', '2007-06-20 11:48:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807435, 533399, 27514, '<td valign="top">so, I''ve been here forever. never have finished like this. <br/>after begging you to enter you finally do and look what happens<br/> <br/>talk about bum luck for me...<br/> <br/>just kidding. I''m proud of you. This kind of recognition of your talent has been a long time coming bright eyes<br/>&lt;3 you</td>', 'so, I''ve been here forever. never have finished like this. after begging you to enter you finally do and look what happens talk about bum luck for me... just kidding. I''m proud of you. This kind of recognition of your talent has been a long time coming bright eyes<3 you', '2007-06-20 11:52:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807477, 533526, 34192, '<td valign="top">In voting I gave this image a 5.  This image is composed well for the most part, but would have been greatly improved had you moved to the left a few feet so the pole was not coming out of his head and so that he would be standing in front of the white background - this would have allowed him to become the focus of the image.  As with your other two posted, the focus here is soft.  I would bet, with the lens you used, that you really cropped this down, resulting in the softness.</td>', 'In voting I gave this image a 5.  This image is composed well for the most part, but would have been greatly improved had you moved to the left a few feet so the pole was not coming out of his head and so that he would be standing in front of the white background - this would have allowed him to become the focus of the image.  As with your other two posted, the focus here is soft.  I would bet, with the lens you used, that you really cropped this down, resulting in the softness.', '2007-06-20 12:01:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807531, 534774, 51793, '<td valign="top">That sure is a lot of frame. Why would you use so much frame to remove what you were actually taking a picture of?</td>', 'That sure is a lot of frame. Why would you use so much frame to remove what you were actually taking a picture of?', '2007-06-20 12:09:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3807631, 529602, 68214, '<td valign="top">Im sorry i made a mistake. Photo was taken with kit lens 18-55mm. (18mm)<br/> <br/>Turn it in BW with chanell mixer.<br/>Then I give it some selective colors.<br/>And some dodging and burning.<br/> <br/>It was actually taken in light rain, where I was waiting my friends who were diving just there on the left. <br/> <br/>This photo is dedicated to my ex-girlfriend. I was going throu hard times, and I was thinking (siting on the beach) about my future and saw this two children having a good time. <br/>Miss you baby...<br/>That is way the photo is dark.. :)<br/> <br/>Thx to everyone for votes..<br/>I still cant belive.<br/>njoy:)</td>', 'Im sorry i made a mistake. Photo was taken with kit lens 18-55mm. (18mm) Turn it in BW with chanell mixer.Then I give it some selective colors.And some dodging and burning. It was actually taken in light rain, where I was waiting my friends who were diving just there on the left.  This photo is dedicated to my ex-girlfriend. I was going throu hard times, and I was thinking (siting on the beach) about my future and saw this two children having a good time. Miss you baby...That is way the photo is dark.. :) Thx to everyone for votes..I still cant belive.njoy:)', '2007-06-20 12:20:34.000000', NULL, 0),
