(3809934, 533399, 17148, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot...love it...well done. Welcome to DPC</td>', 'Wonderful shot...love it...well done. Welcome to DPC', '2007-06-20 17:45:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3810063, 533842, 43073, '<td valign="top">Perhaps DPCers haven''t attended an event quite like this one; I have. Many times, in fact. This picture captures what''s there really well, and from an interesting perspective. Composition works well for me, the placement of the singer especially so. The other people don''t bother me; in fact, it would be weirder for me without them. That one is going (or being talked to, or whatever) also doesn''t distract me. For me, it''s all part of the scene, and the chaotic energy of it really works to bring me back into that "kind" of scene, scenes which are always moving. I think this image would get that kind of polar response, on one end from those who experience it, and on the other from those who see it (both are valid, they''re just different perspectives which might help to explain your score). My longest comment ever, I think :)</td>', 'Perhaps DPCers haven''t attended an event quite like this one; I have. Many times, in fact. This picture captures what''s there really well, and from an interesting perspective. Composition works well for me, the placement of the singer especially so. The other people don''t bother me; in fact, it would be weirder for me without them. That one is going (or being talked to, or whatever) also doesn''t distract me. For me, it''s all part of the scene, and the chaotic energy of it really works to bring me back into that "kind" of scene, scenes which are always moving. I think this image would get that kind of polar response, on one end from those who experience it, and on the other from those who see it (both are valid, they''re just different perspectives which might help to explain your score). My longest comment ever, I think :)', '2007-06-20 18:04:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3810122, 529602, 93, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by darasbulba:</b></div><hr/><i> Im sorry i made a mistake. Photo was taken with kit lens 18-55mm. (18mm)<br/> <br/>Turn it in BW with chanell mixer.<br/>Then I give it some selective colors.<br/>And some dodging and burning.<br/> <br/>It was actually taken in light rain, where I was waiting my friends who were diving just there on the left. <br/> <br/>This photo is dedicated to my ex-girlfriend. I was going throu hard times, and I was thinking (siting on the beach) about my future and saw this two children having a good time. <br/>Miss you baby...<br/>That is way the photo is dark.. :)<br/> <br/>Thx to everyone for votes..<br/>I still cant belive.<br/>njoy:) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, it''s a wonderful and playful shot, but you should enjoy it on the front page while it lasts.. Dodging and Burning is illegal in basic editing. :/</td>', 'Originally posted by darasbulba: Im sorry i made a mistake. Photo was taken with kit lens 18-55mm. (18mm) Turn it in BW with chanell mixer.Then I give it some selective colors.And some dodging and burning. It was actually taken in light rain, where I was waiting my friends who were diving just there on the left.  This photo is dedicated to my ex-girlfriend. I was going throu hard times, and I was thinking (siting on the beach) about my future and saw this two children having a good time. Miss you baby...That is way the photo is dark.. :) Thx to everyone for votes..I still cant belive.njoy:)   Well, it''s a wonderful and playful shot, but you should enjoy it on the front page while it lasts.. Dodging and Burning is illegal in basic editing. :/', '2007-06-20 18:14:19.000000', NULL, 0),
