(3832152, 533494, 76198, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club! Great shoe. I wish they''d had these during my converse days - my favorite pair had each panel a different color, though, which was cool. <br/> <br/><b>Pros:</b> <br/> <br/>The colors are working for you, and you''ve captured them well. I like the general idea of the composition (abstracting the shoe by cropping part of it) but I do agree with those who suggest you change the angle a bit and definately keep the top of the shoe - it feels crowded. <br/> <br/><b>Cons:</b> <br/> <br/>The biggest is your lighting; it''s quite harsh and flat. If you could diffuse it somehow and/or add additional lights from the sides I think you''d have a much stronger shot; as it is the shadows on the background are quite distracting and the shoe lacks depth. <br/> <br/><b>The Challenge:</b> <br/> <br/>You were concerned about meeting the challenge, but some of these are so open ended that I think people are pretty interested in different interpretations; from my perspective anyway you met the challenge just fine. <br/> <br/>Overall I''d try to soften your lighting try taking your shots from a bunch of different angles, to see if you can find something that pops a little more.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club! Great shoe. I wish they''d had these during my converse days - my favorite pair had each panel a different color, though, which was cool.  Pros:  The colors are working for you, and you''ve captured them well. I like the general idea of the composition (abstracting the shoe by cropping part of it) but I do agree with those who suggest you change the angle a bit and definately keep the top of the shoe - it feels crowded.  Cons:  The biggest is your lighting; it''s quite harsh and flat. If you could diffuse it somehow and/or add additional lights from the sides I think you''d have a much stronger shot; as it is the shadows on the background are quite distracting and the shoe lacks depth.  The Challenge:  You were concerned about meeting the challenge, but some of these are so open ended that I think people are pretty interested in different interpretations; from my perspective anyway you met the challenge just fine.  Overall I''d try to soften your lighting try taking your shots from a bunch of different angles, to see if you can find something that pops a little more.', '2007-06-25 14:28:11.000000', NULL, 0),
