(3837288, 534117, 61705, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BobsterLobster:</b></div><hr/><i> The photo is processed using HDR, which can have quite a strong dodge/burn effect on a sky. I also slightly adjusted the pure whites to a more pink hue but this is quite subtle. Unfortunately I couldn''t rescue the burnt highlights. I completely agree that the sky is not ideal, I''m quite surprised with the ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ah, that would explain it, thanks for the reply. Didn''t know HDR was legal in basic, that''s handy!<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Laurie.</td>', 'Originally posted by BobsterLobster: The photo is processed using HDR, which can have quite a strong dodge/burn effect on a sky. I also slightly adjusted the pure whites to a more pink hue but this is quite subtle. Unfortunately I couldn''t rescue the burnt highlights. I completely agree that the sky is not ideal, I''m quite surprised with the ribbon!   Ah, that would explain it, thanks for the reply. Didn''t know HDR was legal in basic, that''s handy! CheersLaurie.', '2007-06-26 17:13:54.000000', NULL, 0),
